1
00:00:00,912 --> 00:00:02,712
(Sheldon:)Everything is quantifiable.

2
00:00:02,714 --> 00:00:05,544
(Sheldon:)That French fry? A seven.

3
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:07,750
(Sheldon:)Spider-Man? A nine.

4
00:00:07,752 --> 00:00:11,122
(Sheldon:)The number nine--
oddly, only a four.

5
00:00:11,122 --> 00:00:13,092
(Leonard:)How ridiculous is he?

6
00:00:13,091 --> 00:00:15,121
(Penny:)A hundred.

7
00:00:17,395 --> 00:00:19,525
(Leonard:)Sheldon, you're just
assigning random numbers

8
00:00:19,531 --> 00:00:21,361
(Leonard:)to things based on your opinion.

9
00:00:21,366 --> 00:00:22,936
(Sheldon:)No, I'm not.

10
00:00:22,934 --> 00:00:24,864
(Sheldon:)French fries have
three variables--

11
00:00:24,869 --> 00:00:26,739
(Sheldon:)crispiness, saltiness
and shape.

12
00:00:26,738 --> 00:00:28,208
(Sheldon:)Which is why a curly fry

13
00:00:28,206 --> 00:00:29,636
(Sheldon:)only gets a two.

14
00:00:29,641 --> 00:00:32,711
(Sheldon:)If I wanted curls for dinner,
I'd order a clown wig.

15
00:00:34,112 --> 00:00:37,812
(Penny:)Well, a relationship is more
complicated than a French fry.

16
00:00:37,816 --> 00:00:41,086
(Sheldon:)Not according to the work
of Berscheid, Snyder and Omoto.

17
00:00:41,086 --> 00:00:45,086
(Penny:)Oh, what did those
rascals do now?

18
00:00:45,090 --> 00:00:47,720
(Amy:)They developed the Relationship
Closeness Inventory,

19
00:00:47,726 --> 00:00:50,556
(Amy:)which predicts the stability
of a couple based on behavior.

20
00:00:50,562 --> 00:00:52,132
(Sheldon:)Yeah, not to be confused

21
00:00:52,130 --> 00:00:53,930
(Sheldon:)with the French Fry
Goodness Inventory.

22
00:00:53,932 --> 00:00:56,432
(Sheldon:)That's pure Cooper.

23
00:00:56,434 --> 00:00:58,164
(Leonard:)So, this is accurate?

24
00:00:58,169 --> 00:01:00,239
(Sheldon:)It's been around for 25 years,

